  The IDCT mark, generated from Branding/Logo/XLOGO.svg. Each SVG path carried a
  transform="translate(x,y)" and VectorDrawable has no per-path transform, so every
  one is wrapped in the <group> that does the same job; the path data itself is
  copied across untouched.

  Vector rather than the five PNG buckets the Whaaack! logo needs, because this mark
  is flat geometry with no gradients, and because a single-colour silhouette has to
  be tintable: it is solid black with the eyes, the acorn and the whisker punched
  clean through as holes, so on the About screen's near-black card it would render
  as nothing at all. AboutScreen tints it Cream and the holes let the card show
  through, which is the reversed treatment this logo would get on any dark surface.

  viewportWidth/Height are the SVG's own viewBox rather than its 2228x2092 width and
  height attributes, which only scale that box by ~1.088 and would misplace every
  translate below if used here.
-->
